const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is an OEM battery lower quality than a branded battery?', a: 'No — in lead-acid, quality is set by the specification, not the label. A single factory running 18 lines often builds branded and OEM batteries side by side, so the difference is whose specification and quality gate controls the output.' },
  { q: 'Do I own the design of an OEM battery?', a: 'Yes, under true OEM you own the specification and the brand, and the factory owns the manufacturing. That ownership is what keeps 10 repeat containers matching the first approved sample.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between OEM, ODM and white label?', a: 'It is an ownership split across 3 models — OEM means you bring the design and the factory builds to it; ODM means the factory owns the design and you brand it; white label means you apply your label to an off-the-shelf product anyone can buy.' },
